{"id":"f9cf17a69f068a94","group":"58","path":"58/batch10/58-thm-just-exists.md","title":"Countable Compactness with a Countable Model","display":"thm-just-exists — Countable Compactness with a Countable Model","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-just-exists","aliases":["58-thm-just-exists"],"display":"thm-just-exists — Countable Compactness with a Countable Model","depends_on":["[[../batch20/58-thm-compactness.md]]","[[../batch13/58-thm-lowenheim-skolem.md]]","[[../batch18/58-df-satisfaction.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-just-exists"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-just-exists</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-just-exists — Countable Compactness with a Countable Model"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"416b3745e60b0423\" href=\"?note=416b3745e60b0423\" title=\"../batch20/58-thm-compactness.md\">../batch20/58-thm-compactness.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"f5c91ae1bfe4e751\" href=\"?note=f5c91ae1bfe4e751\" title=\"../batch13/58-thm-lowenheim-skolem.md\">../batch13/58-thm-lowenheim-skolem.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"8b6a90316aad78a4\" href=\"?note=8b6a90316aad78a4\" title=\"../batch18/58-df-satisfaction.md\">../batch18/58-df-satisfaction.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L,T,\\mathcal M\\in V\">\\(L,T,\\mathcal M\\in V\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Theory}(T,L)\">\\(\\mathrm{Theory}(T,L)\\)</span>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"|L|\\leq\\aleph_0\">\\(|L|\\leq\\aleph_0\\)</span>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Model}(\\mathcal M,T)\">\\(\\mathrm{Model}(\\mathcal M,T)\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Univ}(\\mathcal M)\">\\(\\operatorname{Univ}(\\mathcal M)\\)</span> use the exact satisfaction and structure conventions from the dependencies.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}just\\text{-}exists}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{Theory}(T,L)\\land|L|\\leq\\aleph_0\n\\to\n\\left[\n\\exists\\mathfrak M\\in V\\;\n\\bigl(|\\operatorname{Univ}(\\mathfrak M)|\\leq\\aleph_0\n\\land\\mathrm{Model}(\\mathfrak M,T)\\bigr)\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\forall T_0\\in V\\;\n\\bigl(T_0\\subseteq T\\land|T_0|&lt;\\omega\n\\to\\exists\\mathcal M_{T_0}\\in V\\;\\mathrm{Model}(\\mathcal M_{T_0},T_0)\\bigr)\n\\right].\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}just\\text{-}exists}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{Theory}(T,L)\\land|L|\\leq\\aleph_0\n\\to\n\\left[\n\\exists\\mathfrak M\\in V\\;\n\\bigl(|\\operatorname{Univ}(\\mathfrak M)|\\leq\\aleph_0\n\\land\\mathrm{Model}(\\mathfrak M,T)\\bigr)\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\forall T_0\\in V\\;\n\\bigl(T_0\\subseteq T\\land|T_0|&lt;\\omega\n\\to\\exists\\mathcal M_{T_0}\\in V\\;\\mathrm{Model}(\\mathcal M_{T_0},T_0)\\bigr)\n\\right].\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Compactness gives a model from the explicitly quantified finite-model condition, and downward Löwenheim–Skolem gives a countable elementary submodel.</li>\n<li>The countable-language hypothesis is what yields the displayed <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\aleph_0\">\\(\\aleph_0\\)</span> bound.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch20/58-thm-compactness.md"